WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.400
When it comes to something
as life-and-death important

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.120
as what to feed ourselves
and our families,

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.760
we should rely not on
anecdotes, but on facts.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.320
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.640
Today, we look at new research

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.080
that reveals why we should steer clear
of consuming chlorella and spirulina.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.320
Here’s our first story.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.680
Schizochytrium,
the type of algae

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.320
used to make
algae-based DHA supplements

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.060
is grown
under controlled conditions

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.080
and has been found
to be free of marine biotoxins.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.800
The same can't be said
for blue-green algae products,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.440
like AFA,
Aphanizomenon flos-aquae,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.560
a blue-green algae harvested
from Klamath Lake in Oregon

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.360
and marketed
as a dietary supplement.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.240
Studies have shown
this blue-green algae

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.600
can produce
significant levels

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.360
of cylindrospermopsin
and saxitoxin.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.000
Cylindrospermopsin
is a liver toxin,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.960
and saxitoxin
is a neurotoxin,

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.160
listed as a Schedule 1 substance

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.320
in the Chemical Weapons
Convention.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.920
The first big exposé of AFA
was published in 2000,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.240
with microcystin liver toxins
found in 85 of 87 samples,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.760
72 percent exceeding
Oregon State's safety limits

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.720
of one part per million,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.440
which is based on
an average adult

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.240
weighing 60 kg,
about 132 pounds,

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:28.280
and consuming
about 2 grams a day.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:31.280
AFA has the toxigenic genes

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.440
that produce
these microcystins directly,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.520
but when you're harvesting it
outdoors,

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.440
it's almost impossible
to avoid the presence

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.600
of other algae species
that can produce toxins too.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.860
Since their release
on the market

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.720
and after some public inquiries

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.360
about adverse health effects
of these products,

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.280
the producers of the Klamath
Lake blue-green algae products

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.160
have repeatedly claimed
that their products are safe.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.760
Well, okay, maybe not safe,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.000
but at least
has toxin contamination

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.320
below the regulatory limit.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.280
In 2018, dozens
of blue-green algae products

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.920
containing AFA were tested,

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.640
and about a quarter
were close to, or over,

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.040
the regulatory limit,

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.760
though only one
Klamath Lake powder

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:12.480
significantly exceeded the limit

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.040
at nearly three parts
per million.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.360
But in 2020,
two AFA supplements

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.440
tested at closer to
50 parts per million.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.600
At the recommended doses,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.760
that could present
up to 75 times

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.840
the tolerable daily intake.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.320
When those two off-the-charts
contaminated brands

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.280
were tested in the 2018 survey,

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.680
they only had down
about the limit.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.240
This confirms
that there is a potential

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:36.640
for great variability

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.960
between lots of AFA
harvested from Klamath Lake.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.640
So even if a supplement company

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.360
claims their brand
tested under the limit,

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.040
you never know
what their next bottle

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.360
is going to contain.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.440
Other studies have shown up to
the same 50-fold variability

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.280
among batches
of the very same brand.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.480
There was even a case reported

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.920
of a young woman
who died of liver failure

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.560
tentatively attributed
to the prolonged consumption

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.680
of toxic AFA supplements,

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.240
given the levels of the toxins

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.640
the researchers
were able to pick up

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.960
in the liver on autopsy.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.720
In light of the findings,

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.360
the distribution
and commercial sales

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:14.120
of AFA blue-green algae products
for human consumption

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.800
appear highly questionable.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.280
And the irony is that
they are commonly consumed

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.720
for purported "detoxification."

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.640
Here's the latest:

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:27.440
2023, Klamath Lake AFA
continues to be contaminated

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.200
with up to ten times
the upper safety limit.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.640
To minimize exposure
to these toxins,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.520
the researchers suggest
using spirulina

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.080
or chlorella-based products
instead.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:45.280
But are they any safer?
We'll find out next.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.080
Previously I've talked about
chlorella's potential benefits

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.320
for preserving
the immune function of athletes

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.920
and improving some
cardiovascular risk factors,

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.120
such as dropping blood pressures
by a few points

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.960
or lowering LDL cholesterol
about eight points.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.440
Remember that green eggs
and ham study,

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.520
where taking chlorella
with eggs

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.840
appeared to blunt
the rise in cholesterol?

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.480
It may help detoxify
some dietary cholesterol,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.640
but what about the toxins

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.560
found contaminating
many algae supplements?

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.920
Blue-green algae like AFA
can make their own toxins,

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.760
but even if the green algae
chlorella can't,

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.920
when chlorella
is skimmed off the ponds,

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.320
the presence of other algae
and microorganisms

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.840
is unavoidable
and can pose a hazard.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.240
When you actually look
at commercial algae supplements

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.640
under a microscope,

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.960
the provided labels
are usually inaccurate

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:35.640
as factual contents
usually do not match.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.400
They may be contaminated
with fungus,

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.240
other algae and bacteria,

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.440
and it seems the contamination
was more frequent

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.120
in the organic
versus conventional products.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.480
One product advertised
as 100 percent organic chlorella

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.960
contained both liver toxins
and neurotoxins.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.320
I've talked
about a case report

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:55.920
of apparent
chlorella-induced psychosis.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.120
There's also been a case
of kidney damage reported

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.320
as well as an apparent
chlorella-induced drop

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.080
in platelet count.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.040
Some reactions
are hard to miss,

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.720
like a whole-body rash
or nausea, headache,

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.360
dizziness, fatigue,
abdominal pain,

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.440
and general weakness

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:12.440
that rapidly resolved
after stopping.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:16.240
In these cases, though,
it was a mixed algae product.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.360
Even without contamination,

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.080
if you cultivate pure chlorella

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.760
it can still significantly
induce DNA damage

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.880
in human cells.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:28.280
Yeah, but those are all cells
in a petri dish.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.000
Yes, but they were
colon lining cells,

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.160
so cells presumably exposed
directly to chlorella

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.880
when you eat it.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:39.960
Though chlorella has been
marketed for "detoxification,"

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.680
it can be contaminated
with toxin-producing algae

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.320
and end up exceeding
safety limits.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:47.040
For more irony,

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.600
chlorella can sometimes
be contaminated in a good way.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.400
Chlorella species
can't make vitamin B12,

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.840
but they may mix with
B12-synthesizing bacteria,

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:59.680
such that if you give chlorella
to some vegetarians and vegans

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.720
with a suspected
vitamin B12 deficiency,

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.800
most seem to get
a little improvement

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.480
in their B12-status.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.280
But after two months
of supplementation,

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:11.400
they were still,
on average, deficient.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.840
Note that chlorella is not
considered to be a reliable,

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.080
sufficient source
of vitamin B12.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.840
The same with spirulina,

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:21.320
which was once thought
to contain B12,

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.960
but it's actually
mostly pseudo-B12,

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.480
a form of B12
unusable by humans

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:29.960
and therefore
not a suitable B12 source.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:34.000
What about spirulina
as a source of toxins?

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.280
I'll address
just that question next.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:41.960
Spirulina is
a microscopic blue-green algae

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.280
whose carotenoid pigments
are responsible

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.760
for the orange-pink hue
of flamingos.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.840
At high enough doses
it can also turn us orange too,

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.720
like if we eat
too many carrots,

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.480
but it's considered benign
and goes away on its own

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.200
when you cut back.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:01.120
The strangest color change
I ran across was this:

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.400
"Green Breast Milk
Following Ingestion

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.360
of Blue-Green Algae."

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.480
Whoa!

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:10.000
But thankfully that also
disappears after stopping.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.520
Spirulina is said to have

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.040
various promising
health effects.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.080
At the same time,
on the contrasting note,

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.000
there are toxins
that might contribute

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.200
to acute poisoning,
cancer, liver damage,

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.120
and gastrointestinal
disturbances,

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.400
with long-term consumption

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.920
potentially leading
to Alzheimer's

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.440
and Parkinson's disease.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:30.000
Okay then.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.360
And those purported
promised health effects,

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:35.480
like playing "a positive role
in treating muscle cramps"

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:36.640
are based on a study

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.160
in which mice were injected
with formaldehyde and vinegar.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:43.440
What can spirulina
actually do in people?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.240
Spirulina can improve
long-term blood sugar control

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.200
in rats, but, apparently,
not in humans.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.600
It's also disappointing

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.160
when it comes
to anti-inflammatory

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.280
or antioxidant effects.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.960
Spirulina may help
lower cholesterol, though,

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.840
perhaps due
to reducing fat absorption

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.760
and lower blood pressures
by four or five points.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:05.960
There was a recent trial

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.080
where mild-to-moderate
Alzheimer's patients

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.557
were randomized
to a gram a day

00:08:09.557 --> 00:08:11.600
of spirulina or placebo
for 12 weeks,

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.280
and appeared to end up
slightly better off cognitively

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.080
than those
in the control group.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.920
So those are some
of the potential upsides.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.320
The concern is that,

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:22.480
although algae supplements
like blue-green algae,

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.560
chlorella, and spirulina

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.520
are all advertised
as being beneficial,

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:27.920
they might be harmful

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:31.760
because they may contain
algal toxins.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:32.880
Though most toxins are found

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.960
contaminating the Klamath Lake
AFA blue-green algae,

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:40.160
some toxins are found in some
spirulina supplements as well.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.440
Spirulina samples tested
from markets around the world

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.480
have shown
highly variable results,

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:50.520
ranging from non-detection
to alarming levels of toxins.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.200
The presence of toxin-producing
algae contaminants

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.680
is the most likely explanation

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.680
for the presence of toxins
in spirulina products,

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.920
because producers
cultivate spirulina

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.040
in open outdoor ponds

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.880
which are vulnerable
to contamination

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:06.120
with toxin-producing species.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:06.920
There have been calls

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.440
for strict quality control
and monitoring,

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.400
but that doesn't seem
to have panned out.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.960
This study examined
what was growing

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.920
in five commercial
spirulina products

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.880
including pills and powders.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.880
Several potentially
pathogenic bacteria

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:21.480
were detected
in the products,

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.120
and algae toxins were found
in all of the products

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.560
at levels that could lead
to consumers exceeding

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.760
the recommended daily limits.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.400
One study of five
protein powders with spirulina

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:34.680
found that four of them
even contained BMAA,

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.320
which is a neurotoxin

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:38.960
linked to some progressive
neurodegenerative diseases

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.120
like ALS,

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:43.080
which I've talked about before.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.440
Yet spirulina products

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:48.280
continue to be advertised
as detoxifiers.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:51.160
Though spirulina
is commonly contaminated,

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.960
the levels of toxins
is significantly lower

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.960
than has been found in other
blue-green algae supplements.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:59.320
Nevertheless, there's a concern
that long-term exposure

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.960
to even very low levels
of these toxins

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.880
may increase the risk
of liver cancer, for example.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.440
There are also case reports
of acute liver damage

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.040
tentatively tied
to spirulina intake,

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:13.360
as well as acute muscle damage
and rare autoimmune reactions

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:16.560
to spirulina,
AFA blue-green algae, or both,

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:21.480
including blistering disorders
too disturbing to display.

